Unified CLI for OpenAI-compatible APIs (OpenAI, OpenRouter, APIMart and any
compatible relay), plus local offline models for AIGC detection, OCR, background
removal, depth maps, TTS/ASR, and image understanding.

Generate images, videos and music, run Midjourney, chat with tools, search the
web, fetch pages as Markdown, search prompt ideas and knowledge bases — or
expose all of it to AI agents via MCP.

Choose by task:
  image / video / music / audio   generate or convert media
  image --edit / upscale          edit, inpaint, or upscale an image
  detect / preview --detail       inspect AIGC signals and metadata
  ocr / redact                    extract text or remove PII
  ideas / knowledgebase           search prompts or local documents
  chat / mcp                      chat with tools or expose tools to an agent

Chat is the default command when no subcommand is given: bare aigc-cli opens
the interactive TUI, positional text sends a single message, and chat flags
such as -p/--save/--session work without typing the "chat" subcommand.

Getting started (no config file required):
  1. Credentials:  export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx
                   export OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.apimart.ai   # any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
                   (or per-command flags --api-key/--api-base; Ollama/local needs no key)
  2. Inspect:      aigc-cli --print-config                # effective config as YAML
  3. Run:          aigc-cli image --prompt "A cat" --dry-run   # preview request, zero cost

Persistent config lives at ~/.config/aigc-cli/config.yaml and must already exist
 (copy docs/*/examples/config.yaml). Then write values with:
   aigc-cli config set api_key sk-xxx --force
   aigc-cli config set defaults.image.model gpt-image-2

Models: image and video have no built-in model — pass --model or set
 defaults.<cmd>.model in config.yaml. Other commands apply their own default.
 Run 'aigc-cli models' to list what the current endpoint offers.

Offline commands (detect, ocr, background, depth, upscale, vision, audio, ideas,
 knowledgebase) need a one-time model download: run 'aigc-cli <command> init'.
 redact works offline out of the box; its optional ONNX model can be installed
 with 'aigc-cli redact init --model zh-pii'.

Output & exit: generated/downloaded files go to -o/--output (default ".").
 Results print as text; -v adds the full request/result JSON; --print-config is
 YAML. Exit code 0 = success, 1 = error (message on stderr).

Guides: docs/zh/ (中文) and docs/en/ (English) are authoritative. Run
'aigc-cli <command> --help' for command-specific flags.

Usage:
  aigc-cli [message] [flags]
  aigc-cli [command]

Examples:
# Setup (env vars need no config file)
  export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx
  export OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.apimart.ai
  aigc-cli --print-config                                 # show effective config

# Chat is the default command when no subcommand is given
  aigc-cli                                               # interactive chat (TUI)
  aigc-cli --save                                        # interactive chat + session
  aigc-cli "Hello, who are you?"                         # one-shot message
  aigc-cli -p "Hello, who are you?" --dry-run            # preview the request
  echo "Translate this" | aigc-cli -p "en to zh"         # piped stdin + instruction

# Common workflows
  aigc-cli image --prompt "A cat under starry sky"
  aigc-cli video --prompt "A kitten yawning at the camera"
  aigc-cli chat --message "Hello, who are you?"
  aigc-cli midjourney imagine --prompt "a cute cat --ar 16:9"
  aigc-cli detect photo.png
  aigc-cli mcp

# Diagnostics — --dry-run/--json are per-command flags, not global
  aigc-cli image --prompt "A cat" --dry-run              # print equivalent curl, zero cost (also video/chat/depth; midjourney/music/audio: on their subcommands)
  aigc-cli image --json '{"prompt":"a red fox","n":4}'   # pass request as JSON (image/video/chat/midjourney/music)
  aigc-cli image --prompt "A cat" -v                     # verbose debug output (full result JSON + token/cost stats)

# Agent integration and guides
  aigc-cli mcp --list-tools                              # list MCP tools (--list-prompts for workflow prompts)
  # docs/zh/ and docs/en/ guide-*.md files are the authoritative reference

Available Commands:
  audio         Audio operations (also: voice)
  background    Remove or replace image background using AI (also: bg)
  balance       Query API key or user account balance
  chat          Chat with AI models (streaming by default)
  config        Read or edit the config file (get/set/list)
  decision      Run typed decision questions (choice / yes-no / score) against text
  depth         Convert image/video to grayscale depth map (offline ONNX)
  detect        Detect watermarks, metadata, and AIGC signals in images
  fetch         Fetch a URL/local file as Markdown, or save a media URL to a file
  ideas         Search AI image prompt ideas (also: idea)
  image         Generate images (also: img)
  knowledgebase Local knowledge base management (also: kb)
  mcp           Start MCP server for AI agent integration
  midjourney    Midjourney image generation (also: mj)
  models        List available AI models (also: model)
  music         AI music generation (APIMart suno/flowmusic, OpenRouter Lyria-3, Bailian Fun-Music)
  ocr           OCR text recognition (offline ONNX or online document parser)
  preview       Preview images and videos (also: pr, --detail for metadata, --describe to set caption)
  redact        Detect and redact PII in text, Word, PDF and images
  search        Search the web and print the provider's raw JSON response
  task          Query task status and result
  upscale       Upscale image resolution with a local AI super-resolution model (offline ONNX)
  version       Print the version information
  video         Generate videos (text/image-to-video, remix, GIF/MP4)
  vision        Local image understanding: describe images offline

Flags:
      --api-base string          API base URL (env: OPENAI_BASE_URL)
      --api-key string           API key (env: OPENAI_API_KEY)
      --config string            path to config file (must exist; default ~/.config/aigc-cli/config.yaml)
      --context-size int         Input context window in tokens (0 = auto-detect from the model). Auto-compacts near the window while keeping recent messages.
      --dry-run                  Print the equivalent curl without calling the API
      --http-proxy string        HTTP proxy URL (env: HTTP_PROXY / HTTPS_PROXY / NO_PROXY)
      --inject-json string       JSON object merged additively into the request body (arrays append, scalars overwrite); JSON string or file path
      --interactive              Enter interactive multi-turn chat mode
      --json string              JSON file, string, or "-" for stdin
      --keep-recent-tokens int   Recent tokens kept verbatim after compaction (0 = default 20000)
      --list-sessions            List saved chat sessions and exit (newest 20 by default)
      --max-output int           Maximum tokens in response
      --message stringArray      User message (repeatable; an existing file path is read as the message)
  -m, --model string             Model name (overrides defaults.{cmd}.model; required by image/video when unset)
      --name string              Session name (requires --save or --session; renames on resume)
      --no-auto-compact          Disable automatic context compaction (manual /compact still works)
      --no-proxy                 ignore http_proxy config and HTTP_PROXY / HTTPS_PROXY for this run (direct connection)
      --no-skills                Disable skills discovery and loading
      --no-stream                Disable streaming, wait for full response
      --no-tui                   Never open the interactive TUI; require -p/--message or piped stdin
  -o, --output string            output directory for downloaded/generated files (default ".")
      --print-config             show effective configuration and exit
  -p, --prompt stringArray       Alias for --message (repeatable; an existing file path is read)
  -P, --provider string          Named provider from config.providers (overrides defaults.{cmd}.provider)
      --reserve-tokens int       Tokens reserved below the context window for output and tool schemas (0 = default 16384)
      --save                     Save this chat as a JSONL session (default dir: ~/.config/aigc-cli/sessions)
      --search-provider string   Third-party vendor name for the web_search/web_fetch tools: duckduckgo/firecrawl/brave/doubao/deepseek/exa/wsa (overrides defaults.search.provider)
      --session string           Resume a session by id or JSONL file path (implies saving)
      --session-dir string       Session directory (default ~/.config/aigc-cli/sessions)
      --session-limit int        Max sessions shown by --list-sessions (0 = all) (default 20)
      --skill stringArray        Load a skill file or directory (repeatable)
  -s, --system string            System prompt to set AI behavior
  -t, --temperature float        Sampling temperature (0-2)
      --timeout int              HTTP request timeout in seconds; also caps async task polling (overrides config timeout / defaults.<cmd>.timeout)
  -v, --verbose                  verbose debug output
  -y, --yes                      Auto-approve confirm-gated tools in both TUI and non-interactive mode
      --zdr                      request zero data retention where supported (OpenRouter chat/music)

Use "aigc-cli [command] --help" for more information about a command.
